49
00:03:34,452 --> 00:03:38,817
For Part 3, from the course root,
you run the generator of variant A.

50
00:03:38,857 --> 00:03:43,222
It prints the path of the sandbox,
a sealed room on your own machine.

51
00:03:43,262 --> 00:03:46,797
Inside it, you open the lab
shell, and read SYMPTOMS.md.

52
00:03:47,137 --> 00:03:51,844
You do not read generate.sh, which
is the answer to "what happened".

53
00:03:51,884 --> 00:03:56,380
You do not read check.sh, which
lists the end state line by line.

54
00:03:56,420 --> 00:04:02,243
You keep a log of every command. When you
think you're done, you run check.sh, which

55
00:04:02,283 --> 00:04:05,872
prints PASS, or NOT YET with
one line per condition.

56
00:04:06,212 --> 00:04:11,647
The generator runs with the fixed lab clock,
so the commit IDs in your sandbox equal

57
00:04:11,687 --> 00:04:17,123
the IDs in the answer key. Commits that you
make in the lab shell use the real clock

58
00:04:17,163 --> 00:04:19,860
and get different IDs. Video 1 showed why.

59
00:04:20,200 --> 00:04:25,163
Part 4 needs a second person or the tutor,
who asks each question, waits for the

60
00:04:25,203 --> 00:04:28,853
answer, asks the follow-up, and
scores with the answer key.

61
00:04:28,893 --> 00:04:33,606
If you rehearse alone, record yourself
and score the recording the next day.

62
00:04:33,946 --> 00:04:38,677
The examiner scores with the answer key.
You do not open the key yourself before the

63
00:04:38,717 --> 00:04:39,529
gate is scored.

64
00:04:39,869 --> 00:04:45,088
How the hands-on part is scored. Three
ways. The end state: check.sh inspects the

65
00:04:45,128 --> 00:04:49,632
sandbox with read-only commands, and
each failed line costs one point.

66
00:04:49,672 --> 00:04:54,955
The safety of the path: your command log
is read for evidence before change, a way

67
00:04:54,995 --> 00:05:00,213
back before each rewrite, and no command
that could destroy uncommitted or shared

68
00:05:00,253 --> 00:05:05,406
work where a safer one exists. And the
explanation: what SYMPTOMS.md asks you to

69
00:05:05,446 --> 00:05:10,535
write, with root causes in the form of
the root-cause box of Chapter 1, section

70
00:05:10,575 --> 00:05:10,859
1.10.

71
00:05:11,199 --> 00:05:15,434
After a miss. A miss is not a verdict
on you. It leads to remediation and a

72
00:05:15,474 --> 00:05:18,341
different variant. It does
not lead to the answers.

73
00:05:18,381 --> 00:05:22,501
The examiner gives you your score
sheet, and nothing from the answer key.

74
00:05:22,541 --> 00:05:27,289
You use the remediation map at the end of
the gate file: for every item on which you

75
00:05:27,329 --> 00:05:31,963
lost more than a third of the points, you
restudy the listed sections and redo the

76
00:05:32,003 --> 00:05:33,444
labs of the listed module.

77
00:05:33,784 --> 00:05:38,964
You retake the whole gate after at least
two days. Parts 1, 2 and 4 are asked again,

78
00:05:39,004 --> 00:05:44,121
